# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.log

# Virtual environments
# NOTE: narrowed from a bare `bin/` (2026-07-05) — that pattern matched ANY
# directory literally named `bin` anywhere in the tree, which silently
# swallowed services/telegram-gateway/bin/run_telegram_bot.py (a REAL,
# never-versioned launchd entrypoint containing the Telegram single-poller
# flock guard) for its entire history. Scope to actual venv bin dirs only.
# The DIRECTORY ITSELF, not just its contents.
#
# This read `.venv/bin/` and `venv/bin/`, which ignores what is INSIDE a venv but
# not a path NAMED .venv. On 2026-09-26 a symlink `.venv -> <live tree>/.venv` was
# created in a worktree, `git add -A` therefore TRACKED it, and merging the branch
# replaced the live tree's real .venv DIRECTORY with that symlink — which then
# pointed at itself. The running backend survived only because it had already
# loaded its interpreter; the next restart would have failed.
.venv
venv
.venv/
venv/
env/bin/
include/
Include/
lib/
lib64/
Scripts/
pyvenv.cfg

# Exception: Allow project scripts directory (not venv Scripts/)
!scripts/

# Jupyter / system folders
**/share/
**/etc/

# Databases
*.db
chat.db
chats.db
# Runtime data dir (live SQLite + timestamped backups like chats.db.backup_*,
# which don't match *.db). Prevents committing live conversation data.
/data/

# Node.js
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm
.yarn-integrity

# React build
react-ui/build/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.docker
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
.env.backup*

